### 1.1 Licensor

"Licensor" means the individual or entity identified in the accompanying application or project notices as offering the Software under this License, acting only with respect to rights that individual or entity owns or is authorized to license.

For a Contribution, the "Receiving Licensor" means the project Licensor to whom the Contribution is intentionally submitted for inclusion. A recipient of a copy, or an operator of a fork, does not become the Receiving Licensor merely by possessing, modifying, or hosting the Software.

### 1.2 You

"You" and "Your" refer to the individual or entity exercising rights under this License. Rights for Personal Use are granted only to natural persons. Entities may exercise the express technical-research and contribution permissions in Sections 2.2, 2.3, and 12, but receive no general right to organizational or Commercial Use.

### 1.3 Software

"Software" means the source code, executable code, documentation, assets, configuration files, and other materials expressly made available under this License, including Contributions incorporated under Section 12.

Third-party materials identified as governed by another license are excluded and remain governed by their respective licenses. Independently created user data and outputs are not Software merely because they were entered into, processed by, or generated using the Software. This exclusion does not cover copies of protected code, assets, or other materials included in those outputs.

### 1.4 Personal Use

"Personal Use" means use by a natural person solely for that person's own private, noncommercial purposes.

Personal Use excludes use on behalf of any organization; employment, freelance work, professional services, or business operations; providing the Software's functionality to another person; operating it for customers, clients, household members, friends, employees, or other users; Commercial Use; and deployment accessible for use by the public.

### 1.5 Private Modification

"Private Modification" means a modification created and used solely by You for Personal Use and not Distributed or made available to another person. Modifications made for technical research or submission as a Contribution are governed by their separate express permissions, rather than this definition.

### 1.6 Modified Version

"Modified Version" means a version of the Software that has been modified, adapted, translated, extended, combined with other code, or otherwise changed. Combining independently licensed materials does not change their ownership or override their licenses.

### 1.7 Distribution

"Distribution" and "Distribute" mean providing or making a copy of the Software, a portion of it, or a Modified Version available to another person or entity, whether paid or free, public or private, in source or executable form.

Examples include publishing, uploading, transferring, sharing, giving away, selling, mirroring, repackaging, distributing binaries or modified builds, and including covered materials in another distributed product. The express permissions in Sections 2.3, 4, 7, and 12 remain applicable even where an activity involves making copies available.

### 1.8 Service

"Service" means making the functionality of the Software or a Modified Version available for use by another person through a network or shared environment. Examples include SaaS, hosted applications, websites, APIs, public servers, shared cloud deployments, and multi-user installations.

A network installation accessible for use only by its individual licensee is not a Service merely because it uses a network or rented infrastructure.

### 1.9 Commercial Use

"Commercial Use" means use primarily for commercial advantage, monetary compensation, business operations, professional services, or activity on behalf of a business or organization. It may occur without charging users for access.

