## 14. Termination and correction

For Your first material violation, You must immediately cease the violating activity. Your rights under this License otherwise continue if You correct the violation and take practical steps to remedy its consequences within 30 calendar days after receiving written notice from the Licensor identifying the violation.

If You do not complete that correction within the 30-day period, Your rights automatically terminate at the end of that period. A subsequent material violation after correction of the first automatically terminates Your rights immediately. The correction opportunity does not authorize continued violating activity or waive remedies for a violation.

Upon termination, You must cease activities relying on the terminated rights. The Licensor may reinstate those rights in writing only to the extent it is authorized to do so.

Termination does not affect ownership, contribution grants already made, lawful rights of other recipients, rights independently granted by law or third-party licenses, available remedies, or provisions that by their nature survive termination, including Sections 9, 10, 11, 12.4, 15, and 16.

